<section class="hero">
  <h1>choudoufu</h1>
  <p class="tagline">Plenty of state. None of it binding.</p>
  <p class="tagline-sub">Your config says what should exist, the cloud says what does &mdash; no file gets a vote.</p>
</section>

<section class="lead">
  <p>choudoufu is a fork of OpenTofu that adds a stateless mode: no state
  file, no backend, no lock. Ownership of a resource lives on the resource
  itself, as tags, and every plan rebuilds prior state from the live system
  instead of trusting a file.</p>
  <p>Everything else in this fork is stock OpenTofu, unmodified.</p>
</section>

<section class="demo">
  <h2>See it work</h2>
  <p>One command runs the full demo against a local AWS emulator. It needs
  Docker. The exit code is the verdict.</p>
  <pre><code>bash stateless/e2e/run.sh --expect 5</code></pre>
</section>

